---
import Machine from "../components/Machine.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="llmcpu"
  description="A computer whose CPU is a language model: it runs poems, photographs, noise and real programs alike, in your browser."
>
  <div class="intro">
    <h1>A computer whose CPU is a language model</h1>
    <p>
      Give it anything: a poem, a photograph, a tune, a font, a program for some other machine, or noise. Before it
      runs a byte, a small language model writes down the language it thinks the bytes are in: what an instruction is,
      where one ends, what the pieces mean. Then it reads them in that language, a chunk at a time, on a little machine
      with memory, registers, a console and a 32 by 32 pixel display. There is no wrong reading, only the one it
      committed to. Watch it hold to that language, revise it out loud, or quietly drift; watch a program rewrite
      itself as it is read; watch what a photograph or a font draws. The recordings replay real runs on any laptop, and with a GPU you
      can run a model yourself. Hand it a real RISC-V program and a silicon processor can run alongside, to show
      where the two part ways.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Machine />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
  }

  .intro p {
    font-size: var(--step1);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
